{"step_index":253,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T00:50:47Z","input_tokens":2433,"cache_read_tokens":77937,"output_tokens":10555,"thinking":"Consistent package header style is good to maintain. The same clean style will be applied to the `src/visualizacion/__init__.py` file. The next step involves designing and writing the `metricas_pipeline.py` module.\n\n\nEnsuring the `metricas_pipeline.py` module captures all specified metrics, including counts for each lifecycle stage from initial raw records to final labeled records. This encompasses both the geo-spatial audit and rescue rate calculations, incorporating all intermediate data points like candidates outside the polygon, retained records, and corrupt coordinates. The core logic will calculate the rescue rate percentage based on rescued coordinates over corrupt decimal candidates, and the recovery rate percentage for points initially outside the canton.\n\n\nCalculations for geo-referencing effectiveness, retention rates, and overall pipeline effectiveness are needed. These will use defined variables representing intermediate data states. Final dataset metadata, including column counts, data types, date ranges, and unique regions, are included in the module. Structured exports in JSON and Markdown formats will be generated for the audit report.\n\n\nStandalone execution of `calcular_metricas_pipeline` without arguments relies on reading Parquet checkpoints for intermediate counts, calculating excluded and final record counts implicitly. It attempts to load Parquet files for each stage and infers values where arguments are missing, allowing flexible integration within the larger workflow or independent execution with existing data. This addresses the need for flexible usage and data persistence when called without direct input arguments.\n\n\nCalculating missing intermediate counts by loading from checkpoint files when input values are not provided as arguments. The logic determines `n_finales_etiquetados` from the final labeled data and infers values for other stages such as geocoded records (`n_geo_correctos`) from intermediate Parquet files if those inputs are unavailable. Further calculations derive values like `n_descartados_irreversibles` and determine the relationship between retained and rescued records.\n\nThe system will address cases where `n_limbo_retenidos` or `n_rescatados_algoritmo` are missing, either independently or together. When both are missing, it will attempt to identify the difference between initial filtered records and geocoded records to determine the number of records with invalid coordinates that were kept.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"r\"\"\"\nmetricas_pipeline.py — Auditoría estadística integral del ciclo de vida del pipeline (Paso 5.5).\n\nCorresponde a las Fases R 11 y 13 (líneas 507-520 y 617-626) del script original:\n    print(paste(\"-> Homicidios procesados (2010-2024):\", nrow(homi_2010_2024)))\n    print(paste(\"-> Total rescatados perfectos a la primera:\", nrow(geo_correctos)))\n    print(paste(\"-> Total rescatados por algoritmo de texto:\", nrow(listo.corrcion.casos.posibles)))\n    print(paste(\"-> Casos en limbo con coordenadas correctas retenidos:\", nrow(limbo_formato_correcto)))\n    print(paste(\"TOTAL DE REGISTROS GEORREFERENCIADOS:\", nrow(homi_Nueva)))\n    print(paste(\"Efectividad total de la base:\", round((nrow(homi_Nueva) / nrow(homi_2010_2024)) * 100, 2), \"%\"))\n\nObjetivo en Python (Paso 5.5):\n    Consolidar en un solo reporte auditable todo el recorrido de los datos desde el CSV\n    bruto inicial (Fase 1) hasta el dataset etiquetado definitivo (Fase 5):\n      • Conteos globales del ciclo de vida (brutos → post-filtro temporal/insular → finales).\n      • Desglose geoespacial y tasa de rescate del algoritmo reparador decimal (Fase 4)\n        frente a coordenadas descartadas irreversibles.\n      • Efectividad general de georreferenciación (%) sobre el universo continental de análisis.\n      • Metadatos descriptivos del entregable final (columnas, tipos, rango temporal, cobertura).\n      • Persistencia estructurada en JSON (`reports/auditoria_fase5.json`) y resumen ejecutivo\n        en Markdown (`reports/auditoria_fase5.md`) listo para incorporar en la tesis.\n\nEn palabras simples:\n    Es el \"acta de cierre contable\" de todo el preprocesamiento. Demuestra con números\n    verificables cuántos registros entraron al sistema, por qué salió cada registro\n    excluido, cuántos rescató el algoritmo geoespacial y cuál es la efectividad final\n    del dataset que alimentará los modelos de series temporales (Fase 6).\n\"\"\"\n# `asdict` convierte un objeto `@dataclass` en un diccionario común de Python `{clave: valor}`,\n# ideal para guardarlo directamente como archivo JSON.\nfrom dataclasses import asdict, dataclass, field\n\n# `datetime` y `timezone` permiten registrar la fecha y hora exacta (UTC) en que se corrió la auditoría.\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n\n# `json` es la librería estándar de Python para leer y escribir archivos `.json`.\nimport json\n\n# `Path` maneja rutas de archivos de forma segura en cualquier sistema operativo.\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom src.ingesta.config import (\n    INTERIM_FILTRADO,          # Salida Fase 3: homi_filtrado_2024.parquet (universo continental).\n    INTERIM_GEO_CORRECTOS,     # Salida Fase 4: geo_correctos.parquet (1ra auditoría espacial).\n    INTERIM_INSULAR_EXCLUIDO,  # Salida Fase 3: homi_insular_excluido.parquet (Galápagos).\n    INTERIM_RENOMBRADO,        # Salida Fase 1: homi_renombrado.parquet (universo bruto inicial).\n    PROCESSED_GEORREFERENCIADO,\n    SALIDA_AUDITORIA_JSON,     # Salida 5.5 JSON: reports/auditoria_fase5.json.\n    SALIDA_AUDITORIA_MD,       # Salida 5.5 Markdown: reports/auditoria_fase5.md.\n    SALIDA_PARQUET_FINAL,      # Salida 5.3 Parquet: data/processed/homi_final.parquet.\n)\n\n\n# ==========================================================